      "body": "## Motivation\n\nIn `SGLANG_DEEPGEMM_STANDARD_LAYOUT=auto` (default), `_should_use_masked_standard_layout` selects `masked` layout when the estimated workspace fits inside `_masked_standard_layout_memory_budget_bytes` (small-batch decode / CUDA graph) and falls back to `compact` layout on larger prefill batches (or when `SGLANG_OPT_DG_COMPACT_EAGER=1`).\n\nThe two layouts round the post-GEMM1 activation differently: `masked` layout fuses `SiLU * mul` with FP8 quantization in FP32 (`silu_and_mul_masked_post_quant`), whereas `compact` layout materializes `SiLU * mul` in BF16 before `sglang_per_token_group_quant_fp8` (~71% BF16 element bit mismatch between `masked` decode and `compact` prefill on SM100). Switching between `masked` and `compact` across batch sizes breaks batch invariance and prefill-vs-decode equivalence under `--enable-deterministic-inference`.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Return `False` (`compact` layout) in `_should_use_masked_standard_layout` when `SGLANG_DEEPGEMM_STANDARD_LAYOUT=auto` and `get_exec().deterministic.enable_deterministic_inference` is enabled, keeping CUDA-graph decode, eager decode, and large-batch prefill on a single batch-invariant layout while still honoring explicit `SGLANG_DEEPGEMM_STANDARD_LAYOUT={masked,compact}` overrides.\n- Add hermetic CPU unit tests in `test/registered/unit/moe/test_deepgemm_moe_standard_layout_deterministic.py`.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Code Formatting with Pre-Commit](https://docs.sglang.ai/references/contribution_guide.html#code-formatting-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests as outlined in the [Running Unit Tests](https://docs.sglang.ai/references/contribution_guide.html#running-unit-tests-adding-to-ci).\n- [ ] Update documentation / docstrings / example tutorials as needed, according to [Writing Documentation](https://docs.sglang.ai/references/contribution_guide.html#writing-documentation-running-docs-ci).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41718935855](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41718935855)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41718935697](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41718935697)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41718935970](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41718935970)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
